	(text "The exposed pad (41) is the chip's ONLY ground: give it a solid, short path (see FABRICATION-NOTES)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0935d517-73b8-41fc-9e15-c5b176798b65")
	)
	(text "RF chain (V3): SMA J1 -> optional antenna bias -> L1/L5 diplexer FL3 -> one LNA per band (U3 AT2659S L1, U4 ATR2652S L5) -> band SAW -> SkyTraq L-match -> PX100"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "12e50539-a616-44b3-ac22-bf57fb327bc7")
	)
	(text "Test pads on the back (TestPoint_Pad_D1.0mm); TP1-TP3 are on the root sheet.\nR23 and R20 sit between test pads, so LNA and antenna current read as a voltage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.26 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2307509a-3c9c-4ac8-a06b-0278772e98ac")
	)
	(text "Reset RC: R12 pull-up here, C56 drawn at U1 pin 17. BOOT_SEL high = boot from flash (R13), UART idle-high pull-ups (R14/R15)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "26e898eb-923e-4bee-9e00-4ecfa4b879aa")
	)
	(text "FL6 (L1) and FL7 (L5, Abracon ABSTS5A2-210M011M, the twin of SkyTraq's reference TA2471A) are 50 ohm with no matching.\nC36 + L14 and C37 4 pF + L15 are SkyTraq's input matches into the PX100.\nC65 and C72 keep DC off the SAWs if pins 40 and 37 carry a bias (2026-10-27 review, V2 item 5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "48351a74-a600-4469-ba78-9cecf759b4c4")
	)
	(text "SH1 + SH2: Laird BMI-S-202-F frame (16.5 x 16.5 mm, about 15 mm\ninside its pads) with the snap-on BMI-S-202-C cover. Solder the frame\nafter inspection; snap the cover on after the first sky test,\nand off again for rework. Keep J3 and the regulators outside\nits 17.3 mm pad ring. The one-piece BMI-S-102 of the Beetle V2\nfits the same pads (no rework access)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 312.42 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4a0bcda0-7fe5-4e27-ad04-141787d9b9b8")
	)
	(text "LNA supply: +3V3 -> R23 (10 ohm) -> V_LNA rail -> U3 pin 6 VDD (and pin 5 SHDN) and U4 pin 6 VDD (and pin 5 EN).\nC62 (100 pF) and C63 go at U3 pin 6; C68 (100 pF) and C69 go at U4 pin 6: the 100 pF first, within 2 mm, each with its own ground via\n(V2 had all four outside the shield). C73 sits by R23. U3 is drawn flipped so both LNA supply pins face the rail.\nLNA current = V(+3V3 - V_LNA) / 10 ohm, about 9 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5e682115-6adc-44c4-8b6b-346502a5fe13")
	)
	(text "U3: C61 470 pF + L21 7.5 nH per the AT2659S data sheet; RFOUT is matched on chip, C64 blocks DC.\nU4: C66 100 pF + L22 9.1 nH per the ATR2652S data sheet's 1150-1300 MHz circuit (22.5 dB, 0.75 dB noise figure);\nRFOUT needs no match, C70 100 pF blocks DC. Pin 5 (EN) is its enable, high = on, tied to V_LNA (as the Beetle V2's U13).\nActive antenna: fit R21 and R22, leave C61, C64, C66 and C70 off; both LNAs leave the path."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "678e86f0-eff5-469c-8a75-0393b6cbdaf9")
	)
	(text "Decoupling: each cap is drawn on the U1 pin (or VDD_RF pin pair) it serves; place it at that pin on the\nboard. C47 sits at Y1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "95840228-0377-4b31-99e2-78fc63f096b2")
	)
	(text "Core: R11 5.1 ohm into the on-chip DC/DC, L16 2.2 uH to V_CORE, D7 Schottky clamp (DS p12)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "98380050-2160-4667-b114-4f2ea40785c5")
	)
	(text "Antenna supply, drawn top to bottom as placed: JP1 picks the source, R20 (10 ohm) senses its current,\nC60 decouples ANT_DC, and L20 (47 nH) puts the DC on the RF line between D6 and C20.\nJP1 open (default) = passive antenna; 1-2 = ANT_BIAS from U1 pin 9 (45 mA limit); 2-3 = +3V3.\nAntenna current = V(ANT_SUP - ANT_DC) / 10 ohm. D6 limits J1 to +/-3.6 V DC. Place all of it beside J1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9d0cdffe-60a7-4793-ad8a-cb9162686db5")
	)
	(text "PX100-5C-01A (SkyTraq PX100 DS p12 reference; pin wiring as on the TinkerNav PX100 V2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a1513d27-f897-4b70-813d-0c8d2ceba644")
	)
	(text "Decoupling is drawn at the pin it serves; place it at that pin.\nVDD_RF: C53 pin 39, C76 pin 38, C49 pin 34, C77 pin 35, C50 pin 1, C78 pin 2.\nVDD11 net: C41 at pin 16, C40 at pin 23 (V1 had both by pin 23). C74 at pin 14, C56 (reset delay, with R12) at pin 17."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 214.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c2795f9c-8b10-4376-be8e-cc214169414e")
	)
	(text "Y1: Epson TG2016SMN 26 MHz (X1G0054410304), +/-0.5 ppm, the\nstand-in for the unstocked TG2520SMN (same family and data),\n2.0 x 1.6 mm centred on the 2520 lands. Fed by the\nPX100's own TCXO LDO (pin 3). Its long side is the\ng-sensitive X axis (0.4 ppb/g typ): keep it along board x,\nacross the thrust. C48 is a 0 ohm link: the TCXO drives TCXO_I\ndirectly, as in SkyTraq's reference (refit 1 nF if the clock fails).\nY2: 32.768 kHz, no load capacitors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fc434aa1-1d30-4652-a361-1c5b15b24a9a")
	)
